  "annotation": {
    "schema_version": 5,
    "type": "bugfix",
    "problem": [
      {
        "text": "The default EXL3 forward dispatch selected full weight reconstruction at exactly 32 flattened input rows. The patch moves that boundary from >= 32 to > 32.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_af3c23f86eab4124a5b8c577ac22e547"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": [
      {
        "text": "Keeping 32-row inputs on the quantized GEMM path is consistent with its existing dispatch tiers: several devices select a 32-row kernel, while Hopper and Blackwell distinguish rows above 32. Avoiding reconstruction at this boundary is a plausible rationale, not a demonstrated performance result.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_94ad1e2fe78d48a2824d6f5f901c8469",
          "call_af3c23f86eab4124a5b8c577ac22e547"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "text": "Only the default choice at 32 rows changes; explicit reconstruct=True or False continues to override the threshold.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_b68bb3135591400db28d1750950ee7fa",
          "call_af3c23f86eab4124a5b8c577ac22e547"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "source_notes": [
      {
        "text": "The existing test compares explicitly forced quantized and reconstructed paths, including batch sizes 31, 32 and 33. It does not exercise default threshold selection.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_a88180761a6b42269f1d404b1eb96d4f"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "No CUDA kernels or repository tests were executed; speed, numerical equivalence and device-specific success remain unmeasured.",
      "The scalar check models Python dispatch only, not tensor reshaping, reconstruction or GPU arithmetic."
    ],
    "links": [],
    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "quantized-inference",
        "title": "Keep exactly 32 rows on quantized GEMM",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "LinearEXL3.forward first reshapes input to (-1, in_features), so 32 counts flattened activation rows rather than necessarily the batch dimension. Both paths apply the input Hadamard transform and retain output reshaping, bias addition and dtype handling.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_b68bb3135591400db28d1750950ee7fa"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The reconstructed path allocates an in_features \u00d7 out_features FP16 weight tensor, decodes the trellis through ext.reconstruct, then uses ext.hgemm, a cuBLAS half-precision matrix multiply. The quantized alternative passes the trellis directly to ext.exl3_gemm, avoiding that full weight allocation. Output transforms are fused when packed output signs are supplied, or applied separately for unpacked output scales.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_b68bb3135591400db28d1750950ee7fa",
              "call_b1543f1d96a14fc3bae1d9f947a7251d",
              "call_f73fe2d1280044aca35805cddccdcb57",
              "call_94ad1e2fe78d48a2824d6f5f901c8469"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The selected native path still has its own preconditions: exl3_gemm checks half-precision activations/output and packed tensor shape relationships; launch requires dimensions divisible by the chosen kernel tiles and supports bitrates 1 through 8. The threshold change does not relax those constraints.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_94ad1e2fe78d48a2824d6f5f901c8469",
              "call_af3c23f86eab4124a5b8c577ac22e547"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A standard-library transcription checked row counts 1 through 4096: only 32 changed default branch, while explicit Boolean overrides remained unchanged. At 31, 32 and 33 rows the new reconstruction defaults were False, False and True.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_d510b1e277dd437eb2ab6b5d6d55a09d"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "findings": [],
    "summary": "Changes EXL3's default reconstruction threshold so exactly 32 flattened input rows use quantized GEMM; explicit overrides remain unchanged."
  },
